  "articleBody": "Planning to finish your lower level starts long before framing lumber arrives. Getting the layout right means accounting for immovable physical elements right away. \n\nWhat to Prepare Before You Start:\n- Structural supports: Note existing load-bearing posts and beam heights, as shifting them requires engineering review.\n- Mechanical clearances: Keep direct, unimpeded access paths around water heaters, furnaces, and electrical panels.\n- Moisture status: Inspect foundation walls and slab areas for dampness or water intrusion before planning finished rooms.\n- Natural lighting and safety: Identify existing window locations to determine where bedrooms can legally go based on egress needs.\n- Future utility lines: Map out rough plumbing for planned bathrooms or wet bars before locking in the floor plan.\n\nIf your layout involves moving support posts or altering exterior window openings, professional planning is critical to prevent code and structural issues. Abraham Becerra and the crew at HH Remodeling LLC provide hands-on custom design support across the Denver metro area. Call 303-505-0866 to review your basement layout.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-23"
}